From b9956f29861239e5298daf715801197c908fe5cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Pires <bruno@blastersystems.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:19:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 124/124] glm cuda: TF_GLM_SAMPLE_ROOT=1 sends a verify step's
 sampled rows to rank 0 alone, one grouped send a follower

Opt-in, off by default. A sampled draw makes its rows whole with a broadcast a row a rank of that rank's vocabulary
span (cuda_sampler Spread), so every rank receives every row: rows x world NCCL calls a round (24 at eight rows and
three ranks), the bytes growing with the world. In a verify step (Engine.verify, verifyShared) only rank 0 reads the
draws: a follower runs with discard_draws and leaves its tokens on the device. With the switch, a verify step's
sampled rows go to rank 0 alone: each follower sends its contiguous [rows][span] logits in one ncclSend, rank 0
receives each follower's block into a stage (one ncclRecv a follower, in one group) and copies it into its columns
of the full rows (cuMemcpy2DAsync); rank 0 then draws as before. Same logits in the same columns, so the same draw.

Every other draw keeps the broadcasts: prefill, chunk, redraw and draft steps draw on every rank (each keeps its own
tokens), and structured output and prompt logprobs read whole rows everywhere. The choice is Engine.in_verify (set by
verify and verifyShared on every rank: rank 0 sends the step, its followers run the same one) and the setting, which
the fingerprint carries (layout 19 -> 20): ranks that would gather differently refuse before any weight loads.

Tests: cuda_sampler's group at TP=3 against a recording NCCL (one send of the block a follower, one packed receive a
follower on rank 0); cuda_ranks_test's TF_GLM_SAMPLE_ROOT case.
